  "2026-10-18T07:48:03.342Z",codex-agent,"Restored linked PM review run passed 2/2 with zero failures, cancellations or skips. Synthetic majority/diversity checks and the committed learnable-signal outer-loop promotion both pass. Aggregate prediction diagnostics do not expose held-out examples or prediction vectors. The retained real snapshot predicts 108 completed and 106 cancelled on meta-validation, 199 completed and 186 cancelled on final-test; candidate disagreement is zero because all accepted checkpoints are the seed."
  "2026-10-18T07:50:16.520Z",codex-agent,"Bounded npm run test:live rerun passed in 58251.420959 ms on production source 5a142fc38a2591eb464ce63819f32f7101c2a9ef. Dataset digest a4320672ba0d2f20e1aebfba7b9e91de71c95e17a9706700f79dfe163c8aae0c and all original scores, recipes, checkpoints and refusal verdicts are reproduced. Two meta-generations, K=2: all four candidates score 107/214, gain 0, lower bound -0.21778781183411927; none promotes. Majority baseline completed is 211/214 (0.985981308411215). Each candidate predicts 108 completed and 106 cancelled; every one of six candidate pairs and every candidate versus incumbent disagrees on 0/214 (0%). Final before/after 198/385 (0.5142857142857142), majority baseline 384/385 (0.9974025974025974), predictions 199 completed and 186 cancelled. The learner does not beat the baseline. Live receipt now includes these evaluator-produced aggregates; pm-rl-prefix tracks the learner improvement. All budgets, knobs, split identities and the statistical gate are unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T07:53:38.864Z",codex-agent,"Strengthened the committed signal sanity run to match the live programme exactly: two meta-generations, two candidates, 40000 inner evaluation samples, confidence 0.95 allocated as 0.9875 per outer comparison, minimum 10 and effect 0.01. It passes 2/2 focused tests: first candidate promotes with gain 0.0686 and lower bound 0.036740389785077876; generation 2 retains it; final score remains 5093/10000 to 5806/10000. No live rerun is needed for this test-only strengthening. Fresh no-local clone health passes after clone-local merge installation and isolated HOME; only the existing provenance advisory remains. PM histories preserve prior byte prefixes."
  "2026-10-18T08:05:14.802Z",codex-agent,"Review release verification on 3fe565dcb70ff975a7a5c3f9b5b353768af0b577: CI run 39109179890 passes npm run release:check on Node 22 and Node 26 and bun run release:check on Node 26. Every variant passes 613/613, zero failures/cancellations/skips, exact 100% statements/lines/branches/functions over all 35 sources, 295 documented declarations, and unchanged identity, duplication, attestation, audit, packaging and changelog gates. The final stricter sanity configuration also passes the linked PM command 2/2: two generations, K=2, 40000 evaluation samples and the exact live criterion. Eight behavior-only revert proofs now cover the feature; both added review reverts fail with tests retained and restored code passes. Final receipt/test metadata is handed off for an additional exact-head CI run; production source is unchanged from measured live source 5a142fc. Release remains disabled; no items are closed. The real learner remains below the majority baseline; pm-rl-prefix is the open follow-up. Existing global extension version skew, the provenance advisory and disabled automatic PM result recording are retained rather than repaired or bypassed."
  "2026-10-18T09:41:56.517Z",codex-agent,"Review round on PR 84 head 030874d: read all three unresolved threads and the complete newest CodeRabbit review; there are zero open GitHub issues. Branch is nine commits ahead of main and not behind, so no main merge is required. Reusing this feature item to fix canonical reservation/proposal receipt lookup and envelope validation, reject programme ids that collide under the existing bounded lease namespace, and clarify the dataset CLI usage. Prior live evidence and statistical criteria remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T09:42:17.714Z",codex-agent,Corrected the review-round claim to codex-agent after the first claim inherited the harness author. The mistaken claim event remains in append-only history; no history records are rewritten.
  "2026-10-18T09:52:20.236Z",codex-agent,"All three review findings are fixed. Reservation and proposal receipt reads use the SDK-canonical key, validate Decision type and exact body id, treat only expected NOT_FOUND as absence, and propagate unreadable evidence. Proposal intent/completion envelopes now persist id without changing the binding. Programme ids are capped at 20: adding the longest eight-character inner suffix stays within the existing 28-character lease segment; 82 maximum-programme lease identities are distinct, and a real maximum-length run resumes without new jobs. README shows one from-trackers flag value followed by positional directories. Four independent behavior-only reverts each fail 0/1 with tests retained: reserveMeta selects a foreign prefixed reservation and drifts; durableRecipeProposals adopts a foreign completed result; removing only the id-length bound reaches writes for oversize ids; restoring only the README line makes the documented-command build fail. All fixes restored; linked restored verification follows."
  "2026-10-18T09:58:26.605Z",codex-agent,"Restored linked review command passed 6/6, zero failures/cancellations/skips, through pm test --run --progress. It covers canonical reservation/proposal collisions and envelope corruption, the maximum-length real programme plus idempotent resume, README-driven dataset construction, existing real decision-model fallback/replay, and SDK case-folded budget accounting. Build, test typecheck, lint, duplication and docstring gates pass. Running both full release commands with isolated HOME and global/system Git configuration before push; previous live scores and gate thresholds are retained."
  "2026-10-18T10:17:13.734Z",codex-agent,"The duplicate local npm run used Node 26, isolated HOME/Git identity and a memory-backed scratch area. It was deliberately interrupted while still passing corruption/continuation cases because shared-host execution was substantially slower than the existing complete CI runs. Its log is retained as incomplete, with no full-gate passing claim. Complete npm release:check on Node 22/26 and Bun release:check will run on the pushed head in the existing isolated CI matrix at unchanged thresholds. Focused linked verification remains 6/6 and four behavior-only reverts remain 0/1 each. No live-data rerun or statistical changes are needed for these receipt/lease/doc fixes."
  "2026-10-18T10:31:06.431Z",codex-agent,"CI run 39118685929 on 54b2573 reports the same single fixture failure in npm Node 22/26 and Bun Node 26: 616/617 pass. The existing budget test generated exhaust-training-samples and exhaust-recipe-promotions, which exceed the new 20-character programme-id contract; it therefore stopped at meta_programme_id before its expected budget refusal. This early exit also left 99.89% aggregate branch coverage, so all three gates correctly failed. Shortening only these test programme names to their unique first key component preserves every original budget assertion and production guard. The focused linked command is extended to include this complete budget regression. All three review threads were acknowledged and resolved by CodeRabbit itself after code inspection; no resolution requests were made by this author, and the bot did not execute tests."
  "2026-10-18T10:33:04.727Z",codex-agent,"The expanded linked review run passes 7/7, zero failures/cancellations/skips, after shortening only the budget-test programme labels. Every training-sample, proposal-call, promotion, approval-replacement, malformed-charge and pretty-body assertion remains intact. This restores execution of the previously aborted budget branches without changing production code or weakening any check. Four review revert proofs remain valid against unchanged fixed functions and README. Pushing the test-only compatibility correction for a complete rerun of both isolated release gates."
  "2026-10-18T10:52:06.830Z",codex-agent,"Corrected-head CI run 39119714690 now passes npm Node 22 and Bun Node 26 at 617/617 with all four coverage metrics 100%; the complete budget regression and every meta branch pass. npm Node 26 also has full meta coverage but hits an existing native-memory fault fixture intermittently: its failed trainer receipt has OOMKilled false at the strict physical-OOM assertion. No meta assertion fails. Investigating and synchronizing the fault evidence rather than retrying until green or weakening the memory assertion."
  "2026-10-18T11:01:12.427Z",codex-agent,"The native-memory fixture correction passes both direct and restored PM-linked real-container verification 1/1, zero failures/skips. A fixture-only behavioral revert fails 0/1 at the missing durable child-death handshake; restoring it passes. The test observes an actual kernel SIGKILL and Docker OOMKilled=true before releasing an idle failed supervisor, retaining original memory/time caps and every existing refusal assertion. Build:test, lint, duplicates and documentation checks pass: 35 source files, 295 documented declarations. Two release variants already pass 617/617 on 2820234; the complete three-variant isolated release matrix will rerun on this fixture correction. Registry currently reports CLI 2026.10.18; pinned SDK remains 2026.10.13 as required. No live retraining or statistical changes were needed."
  "2026-10-18T11:19:51.055Z",codex-agent,"Source-verification CI run 39121554923 on 798cfe8af45371ddec478e5b8c2e79259be0fce5 passes all three complete isolated-identity gates: npm run release:check on Node 22 and 26, and bun run release:check on Node 26. Each reports 617/617, zero failures/cancellations/skips, all four coverage metrics 100%, 35 required source files and 295 documented declarations; identity, publish attestation, production audit, packaging and changelog checks pass. CodeQL passes. The strict native OOM and deadline test passes in every variant. Four independent review-finding reverts plus the OOM handshake revert fail 0/1 each; restored linked checks pass 7/7 and 1/1. Thirteen behavioral revert proofs now cover the complete feature and review work. A fresh no-local clone passes strict health with merge drivers and isolated identity, retaining pre-existing advisory warnings and append-only history. All three review findings were replied to after push; CodeRabbit resolved them by static inspection without executing tests. Zero open GitHub issues; Greptile trial-ended notices provide no review approval. Real-data and sanity receipts are unchanged. The final documentation/claim-release commit will receive another exact-head matrix run; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-18T11:57:45.340Z",codex-agent,"New full CodeRabbit review of 39e6c5e has two unresolved findings: unsupported recovery guidance/options for ambiguous outer meta leases, and missing shared inner-promotion headroom plus swallowed promotion-budget refusal. Read both threads and the complete newest review body; zero open GitHub issue findings. The branch is clean, ahead of main and not behind. Reusing this feature item for supported operator recovery and fail-closed promotion accounting with real tracker regressions and behavioral revert proofs. Prior acceptance receipts and statistical thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T12:15:15.766Z",codex-agent,"Both new review findings are implemented. MetaRequest and the public command forward force takeover and the actual approval; refusals name the supported meta run command with file, dataset, approval and proposer options. A digest-only holder audit goes to the existing approval before replacing the lease, including before the first programme receipt. Verified live and unverifiable holders still refuse. Shared promotion headroom is (1 + meta_generations * candidates) times the maximum declared recipe steps, stored separately from meta_budget and checked atomically against permitted_promotions. Canonical reserved namespaces consume held headroom once; outside promotions count separately. Core accounting exposes only promoted ids, never Generation bodies or held-out examples, to search. Inner promotion_refused reports specifically naming the approved promotion budget throw meta_inner_promotion_budget, including after an accepted prior generation; non-budget refusal replay remains allowed. Full meta suite passed 22/22; build, test compilation, lint, duplicates and docs gates pass with 35 sources and 295 declarations. Four isolated behavioral reverts each fail 0/1: remove only force forwarding, restore only inner-loop refusal guidance, restore only the old reserveMeta function, or remove only the budget-refusal guard. Every fixed source is restored. The complete feature now has seventeen revert proofs. Pinned SDK rejects a Generation type filter before that custom type exists; certified metadata establishes an empty inventory without changing schema or swallowing read errors. Registry CLI is 2026.10.18; the repo SDK pin remains 2026.10.13."
  "2026-10-18T12:17:47.381Z",codex-agent,"Restored PM-linked review command passes 4/4, zero failures/cancellations/skips, using the repository-pinned CLI with explicit author. The outside-consumption regression includes another loop sharing the reservation prefix but outside its canonical inner namespace, so a broad prefix cannot hide consumed promotions. The full meta suite passed 22/22 and the focused linked run also covers the final pre-publication audit target. Result persistence remains disabled by project policy, so this comment records the receipt. Previous complete release CI on 39e6c5e passed 617/617 in all three variants; the new source has 621 tests and will be checked by both complete commands with isolated HOME/Git identity. No new passing full-gate result is claimed yet. Live and sanity receipts, the promotion criterion, dependency pins and releases remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T12:36:35.608Z",codex-agent,"Source-verification CI run 39126701196 on 268d04a9fdd22960a78d9d675a6c342f29153c74 passes all three complete isolated-identity gates: npm run release:check on Node 22 and 26, and bun run release:check on Node 26. Each reports 621/621, zero failures/cancellations/skips, 100/100/100/100 statements/lines/branches/functions across all 35 declared sources and 295 documented declarations. Identity, publish attestation, production audit, packaging and changelog checks pass; CodeQL passes. Full meta suite 22/22 and PM-linked review regressions 4/4 pass. Four independent new behavioral reverts fail 0/1 each and fixed sources are restored, bringing the total to seventeen. CodeRabbit inspected both fixes at this source head, explicitly did not execute tests, and resolved both threads itself. No author resolution request was made. Zero open GitHub issue findings. Fresh no-local clone strict health passes with installed merge drivers and isolated Git identity; existing advisory warnings remain and tracker history is append-only. Main is unchanged, source worktree is clean, live/sanity receipts and thresholds are unchanged, and releases remain disabled. The final documentation/claim-release commit will receive an exact-head matrix rerun before handoff; no merge or close is performed."
  "2026-10-18T12:42:18.761Z",codex-agent,"Final self-check identified a resume edge in the new headroom contract: a completed outer programme receipt skips reserveMeta, so a pending inner phase can run after the retained reservation loses promotion_headroom. Adding a real tracker regression that interrupts after programme completion, removes or damages retained capacity, and requires refusal before any process job. Retained capacity must be revalidated inside the owner-fenced execution of every unfinished phase; cached completed reports remain read-only. The preceding 621-test source verification remains valid for its exact head, but handoff waits for this additional regression and full gates."
